# Functional style

tirjs is a functional TypeScript library.

- Write pure functions. The same arguments always return the same result.
- Pass data in and return new data. Leave arguments unchanged.
- Model data as readonly objects, readonly arrays, and union types.
- Prefer small functions composed with `pipe`.
- Represent expected failure as a `Result`. Throw only for programmer errors.
- Keep effects (I/O, clocks, randomness) outside core modules. Pass those values in as arguments.
- Do not add classes, `this`, or shared mutable module state.

```typescript
export const rename = (user: User, name: string): User => ({
  ...user,
  name,
});

export const loadUser = (
  users: readonly User[],
  id: string,
): Result<User, "missing"> => {
  const user = users.find((candidate) => candidate.id === id);
  return user === undefined ? err("missing") : ok(user);
};
```

```typescript
// Shared mutable updates do not belong in this library.
user.name = name;
items.push(item);
